.TH SLURM-GPU 1 "February 2026" "slurm-gpu 0.1.0" "Slurm GPU Utilities"
.SH NAME
slurm-gpu \- GPU utilization reporting for Slurm clusters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slurm-gpu
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B slurm-report
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B slurm-usage
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B slurm-stat
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B slurm-show-tres
.br
.B slurm-tui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slurm-gpu
queries sacct, scontrol, and squeue to produce per-job GPU and CPU
efficiency reports, cluster-wide GPU usage summaries, and real-time job
monitoring via sstat.
.PP
Each subcommand is also available as a standalone symlink
(e.g.,
.B slurm-report
is equivalent to
.B slurm-gpu report\fR).
Running
.B slurm-gpu
with no subcommand defaults to
.BR usage .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS report
Generate GPU utilization reports by querying sacct.
Shows per-job efficiency metrics including CPU, memory, GPU utilization,
and GPU memory usage.
When no user or time range is specified, defaults to all users from
the last 24 hours.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-starttime " " \fITIME\fR
Start time for sacct query (e.g., 2025-07-24, yesterday, today).
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-endtime " " \fITIME\fR
End time for sacct query (e.g., 2025-07-24, today, now).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Filter by Slurm partition.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-account " " \fINAME\fR
Filter by Slurm account (comma-separated list).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fINAME\fR
Filter to a specific user.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-allusers
Query all users (default when no user specified).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIJOBIDS\fR
Comma-separated list of specific job IDs to query.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gpu
Only show jobs that request GPU resources.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-idle
Only show jobs with GPU utilization < 50% or GPU memory efficiency < 50%.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Generate summary report grouped by user.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-by\-partition
Generate summary report grouped by user and partition.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-by\-account
Generate summary report grouped by user and account.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Include node and GPU type columns.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Use plain text output instead of rich formatting.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write output to file instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-filter\-state " " \fISTATE\fR
Filter jobs by state: all, completed, failed, pending, running (default: all).
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-gpu\-eff " " \fIVALUE\fR
Only show jobs with GPU efficiency >= this percentage.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of jobs to display.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-by " " \fIFIELD\fR
Sort by: user, job_id, state, elapsed, gpu_eff, gpu_mem_eff, time_eff,
cpu_eff, mem_eff (default: job_id).
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-telegraf
Output weighted averages in InfluxDB line protocol format for Telegraf.
Use with \fB\-u\fR for a single user or \fB\-a\fR for one line per user.
Computes time-weighted averages (weighted by job elapsed time) for completed
and timed-out jobs. Ignored with \fB\-\-summary\fR flags.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output to stderr.
.\"
.SS usage
Show current GPU and CPU usage across the cluster, grouped by GPU type.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Show only nodes in the specified partition(s). Comma-separated list.
.TP
.B \-k
Shortcut for \fB\-\-partition h200ea,education,gpu\-common,scavenger\-gpu\fR.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fINAME\fR
Show GPU usage for a specific user.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show GPU usage breakdown by all users.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Show detailed report with individual node names.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Use plain text output instead of rich formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-telegraf
Output in InfluxDB line protocol format for Telegraf.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output to stderr.
.\"
.SS stat
Monitor running and pending jobs with real-time GPU and CPU statistics
using sstat. Automatically filters to the current user unless run as root
or a specific user is given.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fINAME\fR
Filter to a specific user.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Filter by Slurm partition.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIJOBIDS\fR
Comma-separated list of specific job IDs to query.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of jobs to display. 0 = unlimited (default: 100).
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-by " " \fIFIELD\fR
Sort by: user, job_id, elapsed, gpu_eff, gpu_mem_eff, time_eff,
cpu_eff, mem_eff (default: job_id).
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Include node and GPU type columns.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Use plain text output instead of rich formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output to stderr.
.\"
.SS show\-tres
Display the dynamic TRES (Trackable RESource) ID mappings for this cluster.
Shows how Slurm maps GPU types and other resources to numeric TRES IDs.
Takes no options.
.\"
.SS tui
Launch an interactive terminal dashboard with three tabs:
Report (sacct history), Usage (cluster GPU/CPU overview), and
My Jobs (sstat live monitoring).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Filter by Slurm partition.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fINAME\fR
Filter to a specific user.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-starttime " " \fITIME\fR
Start time for the report tab (e.g., yesterday, today).
.TP
.BR \-\-refresh " " \fISECONDS\fR
Auto-refresh interval in seconds (default: 30).
.PP
.B TUI Key Bindings:
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B 1 / 2 / 3
Switch tab (Report / Usage / My Jobs).
.TP
.B Tab / Shift+Tab
Next / previous tab.
.TP
.B r
Manual refresh (resets countdown).
.TP
.B p
Pause / resume auto-refresh.
.TP
.B s
Cycle state filter (all / RUNNING / PENDING / ...).
.TP
.B + / \-
Increase / decrease refresh interval (5s steps).
.TP
.B /
Focus search input.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear search / unfocus.
.TP
.B ?
Toggle help popup.
.TP
.B Up / Down
Navigate table rows.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump to first / last row.
.\"
.SS completions
Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, elvish, or powershell.
.TP
.I SHELL
The target shell (required). One of: bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
slurm-gpu completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/slurm-gpu
slurm-gpu completions zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_slurm-gpu"
slurm-gpu completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/slurm-gpu.fish
.fi
.RE
.SH EFFICIENCY METRICS
.TP
.B TimeEff
Elapsed time / requested time limit.
.TP
.B CPUEff
Total CPU time used / (elapsed time * allocated CPUs).
.TP
.B MemEff
Maximum RSS / requested memory.
.TP
.B GPUEff
Average GPU utilization percentage reported by the GPU driver.
.TP
.B GPUUtil
Raw GPU utilization (can exceed 100% for multi-GPU jobs, shown as sum).
.TP
.B GPUMemEff
Average GPU memory used / total GPU memory allocated.
.TP
.B GPUMem
Absolute GPU memory used.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLURM_GPU_K_PARTITIONS
Override the
.B \-k
partition shortcut. Comma-separated list of partition names
(default: h200ea,education,gpu-common,scavenger-gpu).
.PP
.B slurm-gpu
requires a working Slurm installation with
.BR sacct (1),
.BR scontrol (1),
.BR squeue (1),
and
.BR sstat (1)
available in the PATH.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/slurm-gpu
Default installation location.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show all GPU jobs from the last 24 hours:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-report -g
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show GPU-idle jobs (underutilizing GPUs) for a specific user:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-report -u jsmith --gpu-idle
.fi
.RE
.PP
Summary of GPU efficiency by user and partition since yesterday:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-report -a -S yesterday --summary-by-partition -g
.fi
.RE
.PP
Current cluster GPU usage:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-usage
.fi
.RE
.PP
GPU usage by user on a specific partition:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-usage -a -r gpu-common
.fi
.RE
.PP
Monitor your running jobs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-stat
.fi
.RE
.PP
Launch the interactive dashboard:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-tui
.fi
.RE
.PP
Output for Telegraf/InfluxDB ingestion:
.PP
.RS
.nf
slurm-report -a --telegraf
slurm-usage --telegraf
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHORS
Joe Shamblin <wjs@cs.duke.edu>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sacct (1),
.BR scontrol (1),
.BR squeue (1),
.BR sstat (1)
